; Leave the room through the left exit
;
; Makes the left neighbour (byte $E9 of the room, $80E9) the current room
; and puts Willy on column 30 of the same row: his attribute address
; (#R$85D3) gets column bits 11110. Willy's other state is kept. Pops the
; caller's return address and jumps to #R$8912, which loads the new room and
; restarts the game loop, so it never returns.
; .
; Reached when Willy walks off column 0 (jump from #R$8DD3). Observed in
; the simulator (finding F21).
@label=ExitRoomLeft
c$948A LD A,($80E9)  ;
 $948D LD ($8420),A  ; new current room
 $9490 LD A,($85D3)  ;
@isub=OR COLUMN_MASK
 $9493 OR $1F        ;
@isub=AND ~1
 $9495 AND $FE       ; column = 30 (low 5 bits 11110), row bits unchanged
 $9497 LD ($85D3),A  ;
 $949A POP HL        ; drop the return address
 $949B JP $8912      ; load the new room
